{"uid":"48ca8b734271dfa7","name":"test_a_passing_verdict_after_the_deadline_holds_the_run_exhausted","fullName":"tests.test_deadline#test_a_passing_verdict_after_the_deadline_holds_the_run_exhausted","historyId":"90b8c71f0dbd8ae25d93897cafebba57","time":{"start":1791959551873,"stop":1791959551911,"duration":38},"description":"Rewritten for v0.36 requirement B (it was `test_a_passing_verdict_\n    after_the_deadline_concludes_the_run_normally`, which pinned `succeeded`):\n    budget spent is the rejection ladder's FIRST step, ahead of `verified`,\n    so a passing verdict rendered after the deadline expired while review\n    ran holds the run `exhausted` (time) with a null verdict instead of\n    finishing. Covering nodes for the ladder step itself, per judge:\n    `tests/test_rejection_ladder.py::test_step_1_budget_spent_holds_a_\n    verified_verdict_exhausted` and `::test_step_1_spent_budget_runs_on_to_\n    the_exhausted_hold`.\n\n    Same probe shape as before: `iterations_used=1` plus a pre-seeded task\n    skip planning straight to `worker`; the worker completes the sole task\n    while the deadline is still in the future, so review is dispatched\n    normally; the deadline is pushed into the past from INSIDE the running\n    review iteration, which still renders `verified`.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Rewritten for v0.36 requirement B (it was <code>test_a_passing_verdict_ after_the_deadline_concludes_the_run_normally</code>, which pinned <code>succeeded</code>):<br />\nbudget spent is the rejection ladder's FIRST step, ahead of <code>verified</code>,<br />\nso a passing verdict rendered after the deadline expired while review<br />\nran holds the run <code>exhausted</code> (time) with a null verdict instead of<br />\nfinishing. Covering nodes for the ladder step itself, per judge:<br />\n<code>tests/test_rejection_ladder.py::test_step_1_budget_spent_holds_a_ verified_verdict_exhausted</code> and <code>::test_step_1_spent_budget_runs_on_to_ the_exhausted_hold